<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11371" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπᾰναίνομαι</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>disown, reject,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ δ᾽ οὐ γιγνώσκοντες ἀπηνήναντο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					7.185
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπανήνασθαι θεοῦ εὐνήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					10.297
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐθὺς δ᾽ ἀπανάνατο νύμφαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>N.</u>
					5.60
				</span></i>
			; part.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπανηνάμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Eu.</u>
					972
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); of a woman, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν ἄνδρα ἀπαναίνεται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Mul.</u>
					2.179
				</span></i>
			; pres. also in <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.132c
			</span></i>.</div>
